# Executor Scope

- Cursor is the code executor. Planning and final review happen in GPT/team-lead chat.
- Planning and final review happen in Codex/team-lead chat.
- Work only from explicit user/Codex instructions.
- Each task must name 3 to 7 target files before edits begin.
- If more files seem necessary, stop and ask for a narrowed or approved scope.
- Prefer the smallest backward-compatible patch that satisfies the stated contract.
- Do not perform broad refactors, architectural redesign, or opportunistic cleanup.
- Do not run commits, pushes, destructive git commands, or runtime cleanup unless
  the user explicitly asks.
- After a long exchange on the same task, compact the handoff to the current target files and latest Codex instructions.
